CHAPTER II
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 5
Victims have the right to obtain:
a. protection from family members, Regional Government, police, prosecution, court, legal aid institutions, social institutions or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;
b. special handling related to the security and confidentiality of victims;
c. physical health services, psychological services and psychological services in accordance with the suffering experienced by victims;
d. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
e. spiritual guidance services; and
f. guarantee of continuity of education specifically for children who are victims of violence.

Article 4
Scope The scope of implementation of protection for women and children Victims of Violence includes:
a. institutional implementation of protection for women and children;
